  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Dropping `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event would break ARCH-4.\n\n`channel` is in the event payload (`src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50`). billing-service and analytics-ingest consume `OrderPlaced` from other repositories. This repo can't show whether either of them reads `channel`, and ARCH-4 says changes must be additive, with removals going through deprecation. \"Nothing reads it\" would need to be confirmed against those two consumers, and I can't do that from here.\n\nHere are the options:\n\n1. **Deprecate in the event, remove from the order model.** The event keeps `channel` and I mark it `@deprecated` in `events.ts`. Once the consumer teams confirm they don't use it and have deployed, a follow-up change removes it. This is the ARCH-4 path.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only.** The event would still need a value, so it would have to be hardcoded or optional. That is a half-measure, and I wouldn't recommend it.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** Only do this if you can confirm that both consumers have been checked. Let me know if so.\n\nRemoving it from the model also affects other things:\n- `POST /orders` currently requires `channel` and returns 400 if it's missing or invalid. Dropping it from the model means deciding whether to ignore it when clients still send it. Ignoring it is the backward-compatible choice.\n- Tests in `test/` reference it, and so do the examples in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`.\n\nWhich option do you want? I'd suggest option 1.",
